.context File Menu
.context m.f
.topic File Menu
.topic File Menu

\bFile Menu\p

The File menu has Print and Exit.

Print writes the topic on the screen to a printer or a file.  Exit
leaves PM-DOS Help.

To open the menu, click File, or press ALT and then F.  To choose a
command, click it, or press its white letter.
.context Search Menu
.context m.s
.topic Search Menu
.topic Search Menu

\bSearch Menu\p

The Search menu has Find and Repeat Last Find.

Find looks for text in every topic.  Repeat Last Find, or F3, looks
for the same text again from where the cursor is.

To open the menu, click Search, or press ALT and then S.  To choose a
command, click it, or press its white letter.
.context Help Menu
.context m.h
.topic Help Menu
.topic Help Menu

\bHelp Menu\p

The Help menu has How to Use PM-DOS Help and About.

How to Use PM-DOS Help explains the window, the links and the keys.
About shows the version of PM-DOS Help.

To open the menu, click Help, or press ALT and then H.  To choose a
command, click it, or press its white letter.
.context Print Command
.topic Print Command
.topic Print Command

\bPrint Command\p

Writes the topic on the screen, as plain text, to a printer or to a
file.  A dialog box asks which.
.context Exit Command
.topic Exit Command
.topic Exit Command

\bExit Command\p

Leaves PM-DOS Help and goes back to the command prompt.
.context Find Command
.topic Find Command
.topic Find Command

\bFind Command\p

Looks for text in every topic of the help file, starting after the
cursor.  The topic the text is found in is shown with the cursor on
it.  A dialog box asks for the text, and whether capitals and whole
words matter.
.context Repeat Last Find Command
.topic Repeat Last Find Command
.topic Repeat Last Find Command

\bRepeat Last Find Command\p

Looks again for the text Find last looked for, from the cursor on.
F3 does the same.

Before Find has been used, Repeat Last Find looks for the word the
cursor is on, or the word to its left.  With no word there it asks for
the text, as Find does.
.context Help on Help Command
.topic Help on Help Command
.topic How to Use PM-DOS Help Command

\bHow to Use PM-DOS Help Command\p

Shows the topics that explain PM-DOS Help itself: moving between
topics, finding text, the menus, the dialog boxes and the keys.  F1
shows the same topics.
.context About Command
.topic About Command
.topic About Command

\bAbout Command\p

Shows the version of PM-DOS Help.
.context Find Dialog
.context Find Command Dialog Box
.topic Find Dialog
.topic Find Dialog Box

\bFind Dialog Box\p

Looks for text in every topic.

ÚÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ Find ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ¿
