                                 DEVICEHIGH=
 
Loads a 16-bit DOS device driver into upper memory.

\bSyntax\p

    DEVICEHIGH=[drive:][path]filename [options]

\bParameters\p

[drive:][path]filename
    The driver.

options
    Whatever the driver takes on its line.

\bRelated Commands\p

Upper memory is set up by <\aDOS=\vDOS=\v>.  See <\aDEVICE=\vDEVICE=\v> for what a driver
is, and <\aLOADHIGH\vLOADHIGH\v> for programs.
 
                                     
.context DEVICEHIGH=--Notes
.topic DEVICEHIGH=--Notes
